{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And whenever it was lifted.</b> It says the vav at the beginning of the matter, to say that the matter of the cloud that was upon the Tabernacle served two purposes: one was to cover the tent for honor and splendor, and this is the statement <b>the cloud covered the Tabernacle, the tent of (upon) the testimony</b>, and it further added and said <b>and whenever</b> etc. — meaning, the cloud was also for this purpose, that whenever it was lifted the children of Israel would journey, so that they would know the time of journeying and the time of encamping." "<b>and afterward they would journey</b> etc. One must understand what it means by saying <b>and afterward</b> etc., for it should have framed the decree in the statement in this manner: ״whenever it was lifted etc. they would journey,״ as the measure of the adjacent statement, ״and in the place where it settled etc. there they would encamp.״ And it appears that if it had said ״afterward they would journey,״ it would have been understood that this is the decree of the verse — but that is not the intention; rather, the decree is in the statement that comes afterward: <b>at the mouth of HaShem</b> etc. And this is the measure of the verse: <b>and whenever it was lifted</b> etc., and afterward they would journey etc., and since this is so — <b>at the mouth of HaShem</b> etc. — behold, they journey at the mouth of HaShem." "It further intends to say the following: for otherwise, if it had said ״afterward they would journey,״ the decree would have been in the word ״afterward,״ and the implication would have been that they would not journey beforehand but only afterward, and it would not be conveyed that they would in any case journey whenever the cloud journeyed. Therefore it said <b>and afterward</b>, so that it would be read as a continuation above and the decree would come in the statement ״the children of Israel would journey,״ as though it said ״whenever it was lifted etc. they would journey.״ And if it had said in this order ״whenever it was lifted etc. they would journey,״ then it would have been understood that it is at its lifting that they become obligated to journey, but it would not be evident that if they wished to journey, the non-lifting of the cloud would prevent them. Therefore it said ״whenever it was lifted etc. and afterward״ — to say, and not before."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:04.872956584Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}